From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Select original bounded CPU particle simulation and own atlas allocations
Upstream-base: 0f5a757947b8778b680d4d1ae7e6df1792a514f2

Native simulation uses an explicit constructor tag and shares the original field
initialization, emission, RNG, update, motion and quad bodies. It never registers
a GL handle; native rendering and light submission remain unavailable. Preserve
console construction, services and allocation behavior. The checked host owner
qualifies all templates/specs before publication, owns both original particle
lists, and retains exact authored colours. Guard actual colour indices and signed
frame/angle conversions before the original accesses. Native atlas allocations
are transactional and freed through their owning game arenas.

diff --git a/include/Game/Effects/ParticleSystem.h b/include/Game/Effects/ParticleSystem.h
--- a/include/Game/Effects/ParticleSystem.h
+++ b/include/Game/Effects/ParticleSystem.h
